  "statement": "Table products(id INTEGER, name TEXT, price INTEGER, in_stock INTEGER). in_stock is 1 when the product is available and 0 otherwise. Names are unique.\n\nReturn the name and price of every product that is in stock and costs strictly less than 20. Sort by price from cheapest to most expensive, then by name (A to Z) when prices are equal.\n\nOutput: one row per product, columns name, price.\nConstraints: at most 1000 products, prices are whole numbers from 1 to 1000.\n\nExample\nproducts:\n  (1, 'Pen', 2, 1)\n  (2, 'Lamp', 35, 1)\n  (3, 'Mug', 8, 0)\n  (4, 'Notebook', 8, 1)\n  (5, 'Cable', 19, 1)\n  (6, 'Charger', 20, 1)\nOutput:\nPen|2\nNotebook|8\nCable|19\n\n(Mug is out of stock and Charger costs exactly 20.)",
  "starter_code": "-- Table: products(id INTEGER, name TEXT, price INTEGER, in_stock INTEGER)\nSELECT name, price\nFROM products\n-- Keep products in stock that cost less than 20, cheapest first\n;\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 2000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 600,
